CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 2 --no-por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --graphml-witness /dev/stdout
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
<data key="violation">true</data>
--
^warning: ignoring
<data key="startline">25</data>
--
Thread t takes the lock and sets x, then main takes it and fails the
assertion. The pthread_mutex_lock of main (line 25) has no edge of its own:
only its argument binding was on that line, and it may sit before the other
thread's critical section in the trace.
